he number of rows in the matrix.\"\"\"\n        return len(self._elements)\n\n    def get_column_count(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Returns the number of columns in the matrix, based on the first row.\n        Assumes a consistent number of columns across all rows if the matrix is valid.\n        \"\"\"\n        if not self._elements:\n            return 0\n        return len(self._elements[0])\n\n    def is_square(self) -> bool:\n        \"\"\"\n        Verifies if the matrix is square (number of rows equals number of columns)\n        and if all rows have the same number of columns.\n        \"\"\"\n        rows = self.get_row_count()\n        cols = self.get_column_count()\n\n        if rows == 0:\n            return False # An empty matrix is not considered a magic square.\n\n        if rows != cols:\n            return False # A magic square must be a square matrix.\n        \n        # Ensure all rows have the same number of columns as the first row.\n        for row in self._elements:\n            if len(row) != cols:\n                return False\n                \n        return True\n\n    def calculate_row_sum(self, row_index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements for a specific row.\"\"\"\n        return sum(self._elements[row_index])\n\n    def calculate_column_sum(self, col_index: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements for a specific column.\"\"\"\n        total = 0\n        for i in range(self.get_row_count()):\n            total += self._elements[i][col_index]\n        return total\n\n    def calculate_main_diagonal_sum(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the main diagonal.\"\"\"\n        total = 0\n        size = self.get_row_count()\n        for i in range(size):\n            total += self._elements[i][i]\n        return total\n\n    def calculate_anti_diagonal_sum(self) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the sum of elements along the anti-diagonal.\"\"\"\n        total